<title>FRANCE: CDR says Total sale generates big gain.</title>
<headline>CDR says Total sale generates big gain.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French state agency Consortium de Realisation (CDR) has generated &quot;a handsome capital gain&quot; from the sale of its 1.41 percent stake in energy group Total, a CDR spokesman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The CDR said late on Monday that it sold 3.5 million Total shares. The spokesman told Reuters the shares were sold to several investors and CDR retains 0.40 percent of Total.</p>
<p>Total said it did not buy the shares sold by CDR's unit CDR Participations. CDR was established to take over and sell some of the assets collected by state-owned bank Credit Lyonnais .</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
